  to approach this in a fresh way  for me tennet really is about taking the  uh  the elements of of spy fiction and and  particularly cinematic you know spy  fiction  and having it having new reason to look  at them in a different way taking them  and turning them on their heads really  do you ever come up with ideas  when you're writing a script that even  scare you in terms of not being able to  pull it off  uh yeah i mean the really that's the  challenge i mean as a writer  i try and take my director's hat off and  not be afraid and just say  i want to write the most exciting thing  the most unexpected thing i can think of  for the story  and then i pick up the script again and  put the director's hat back on and go  okay how the hell am i going to do that  and that's when you know you're in a  good place because every film you want  to be challenging yourself you want to  do something different  you

